<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<!--
  Jenkins auto-renders this for any Action attached to a Run that has one. `${it}` is the
  AccessibilityReportAction instance.

  Deliberately NOT using the /lib/hudson t:summary taglib here (even though it's the usual
  convention for this kind of build-page row) - t:summary requires an `icon` attribute, and an
  icon reference that isn't resolvable on a given Jenkins core version (e.g. an Ionicons "symbol"
  name on an older core that only understands classic image-file icons) can cause the *entire*
  tag, including the link inside it, to fail to render. Plain markup here has zero dependency on
  icon resolution, so the link itself can never be taken down by an icon problem - the small
  cosmetic cost is no icon next to the link.

  `escape-by-default='true'` means the *text content* below is XML-escaped on output (irrelevant
  here, no dynamic text content) - the href attribute value itself is written via normal XML
  attribute serialization, which XML-escapes '&' to '&amp;' as required for well-formed HTML/XML.
  That is correct, expected behaviour, not corruption: browsers decode '&amp;' back to a literal
  '&' when parsing the href, so the link still opens exactly the URL Java built. Only a
  *double*-escaped '&amp;amp;' in the rendered source would indicate a real bug (e.g. something
  re-escaping an already-escaped string) - that must not appear here.
-->
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core">
  <div style="padding: 6px 0;">
    <a href="${it.reportUrl}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      📊 View Accessibility Report
    </a>
  </div>
</j:jelly>
